IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch1`
IMPORT `kn-ch2`
IMPORT `kn-majority`
IMPORT `kn-ch3`

-- Mishnah Kinnim: THE SEAT of the person who brought the birds -- a woman after childbirth, a man or
-- woman after a discharge, or anyone who vowed or gave a bird offering.  The tractate speaks of women
-- ("to this one ... to that one"), and Maimonides explains why (Reiss n. 12); the questions are worded
-- for whoever brought the birds.  The priest is an official here and has no seat: what he did is a fact
-- the owner states.
-- This layer holds no rule.  It takes plain facts, builds the law modules' records, and calls them.
-- Nothing here says that any offering can be brought today: Temple offerings ceased in 70 CE.
-- Target compiler: main.
-- GENERATED from tools/kn-seat.l4.in by tools/render.py; edit the template.

§ `Kinnim: questions of the person who brought the birds`

§§ `Where on the altar (1:1)`

@ref Kinnim 1:1
@export Was my offering made at the right place on the altar? Answers yes or no from Kinnim 1:1.
GIVEN animal   IS AN `Animal`   @desc Was your offering a bird or a beast?
      offering IS AN `Offering` @desc Was it your sin offering or your burnt offering?
      level    IS A `Level`     @desc Did the priest make it above or below the red line round the altar?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`was my offering made at the right place on the altar` animal offering level MEANS
    `an offering made at this level is valid` animal offering level

§§ `What I vowed or gave (1:1)`

@ref Kinnim 1:1
@export Did my words make my burnt offering a vow or a gift? Answers from Kinnim 1:1.
GIVEN words IS A `Words of dedication` @desc Did you say "I take a burnt offering upon me" (it is upon me), or "this one is a burnt offering" (this one is)?
GIVETH A `Ground of the offering`
`did my words make a vow or a gift` words MEANS
    `what words of dedication make the offering` words

@ref Kinnim 1:1
@export My vowed or given bird died or was stolen before it was offered: must I bring another? Answers yes for a vow and no for a gift (Kinnim 1:1); for an obligation the text does not say.
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of the offering` @desc Was the bird brought for a vow, as a gift, or for an obligation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`must I replace my bird that died or was stolen` ground MEANS
    `the owner must replace it if it died or was stolen` ground

§§ `My birds were mixed with others, and the priest asked first (1:2 to 1:4, 3:5)`

@ref Kinnim 1:2-1:4
@export My birds were mixed with other birds before they were offered, and the priest asked how to offer them: how many of all the birds may still be offered? Answers from Kinnim 1:2 to 1:4; the rest must die.
GIVEN `designated sin offerings`   IS A NUMBER @desc How many birds in the mixture had already been made sin offerings (by their owner when buying, or by the priest)?
      `designated burnt offerings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many birds in the mixture had already been made burnt offerings?
      `my pairs`                 IS A NUMBER @desc How many pairs did you bring for your obligation without saying which bird was which? 0 if none.
      `the other pairs`          IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each other owner (or other reason) whose unassigned pairs are in the mixture, how many pairs.
      `bought jointly`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the owners of the unassigned pairs buy their birds together?
      `gave the price to the priest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the owners of the unassigned pairs give the priest the money for their birds instead?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` `designated sin offerings` `designated burnt offerings` `my pairs` `the other pairs` `bought jointly` `gave the price to the priest` MEANS
    IF     `the priest may assign each bird to whichever woman he wishes` `bought jointly` `gave the price to the priest`
       AND `designated sin offerings` EQUALS 0
       AND `designated burnt offerings` EQUALS 0
        THEN `the birds in the mixture` m
        ELSE `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` m
    WHERE
        m MEANS `Mixture` WITH
                    `designated sin offerings`   IS `designated sin offerings`
                    `designated burnt offerings` IS `designated burnt offerings`
                    `unassigned obligations`     IS map `a nest of pairs` (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p GREATER THAN 0) (`my pairs` FOLLOWED BY `the other pairs`))

@ref Kinnim 3:5
@export Part of my obligation had been offered when a bird already made a sin or burnt offering fell among the birds I still owed, and the priest asked: how many of those birds may be offered? Answers from Kinnim 3:5.
GIVEN `the bird that fell in`  IS AN `Offering` @desc Was the bird that fell among yours a sin offering or a burnt offering?
      `sin offerings I still owe`  IS A NUMBER @desc How many sin offerings do you still owe from the birds left?
      `burnt offerings I still owe` IS A NUMBER @desc How many burnt offerings do you still owe from the birds left?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many may be offered when a designated bird fell among what I still owe` `the bird that fell in` `sin offerings I still owe` `burnt offerings I still owe` MEANS
    `the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `the bird that fell in` `sin offerings I still owe` `burnt offerings I still owe`

§§ `A bird flew (2:1 to 2:5): only for someone whose bird flew or died`

@ref Kinnim 2:1
@export One bird of my pair, not yet assigned to its offering, flew off or died: what now? Answers from Kinnim 2:1.
GIVEN where IS A `Where the bird went` @desc Did it fly into the air, fly among birds that must die, die, or fly among other birds waiting to be offered?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of the flight`
`what now that one bird of my pair has gone` where MEANS
    `what follows when a bird of an unassigned pair goes` where

@ref Kinnim 2:2
@export I brought two pairs and another woman two, and a bird flew between them: how many pairs, of the four, can still be offered? Answers from Kinnim 2:2.
GIVEN `one-way flights` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times did a bird fly from one woman's pairs to the other's (there and back is two)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of our four pairs can still be offered` `one-way flights` MEANS
    `nests still offerable when two women had two nests each` `one-way flights`

@ref Kinnim 2:3
@export My pairs stood in a row with other women's pairs, and a bird flew down the row to the end and back: how many of my pairs can still be offered? Answers from Kinnim 2:3, as Bartenura reads it.
GIVEN `the pairs in the row`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc How many pairs each woman had, in the order they stood, starting from where the bird first flew from.
      `my place in the row`   IS A NUMBER @desc Your place in the row, counting the first as 1.
      `round trips`           IS A NUMBER @desc How many times the bird flew to the end of the row and back.
      `as some say`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Answer as "some say" in 2:3 (the last woman loses nothing once the one before her has nothing)? The halakha is the first view (false).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of my pairs in the row can still be offered` `the pairs in the row` `my place in the row` `round trips` `as some say` MEANS
    at (`the nests left after round trips` `the pairs in the row` `round trips` `as some say`) (`my place in the row` MINUS 1)

@ref Kinnim 2:4
@export My unassigned pair stood beside a pair already assigned whose two birds had been mixed, and a bird flew between them: what now? Answers from Kinnim 2:4.
GIVEN what IS A `Flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` @desc Which flight happened?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of the flight`
`what now that a bird flew between my pair and an assigned pair` what MEANS
    `what follows a flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` what

@ref Kinnim 2:5
@export My unassigned pair stood between sin offerings and burnt offerings, and its birds flew: what now? Answers from Kinnim 2:5.
GIVEN what IS A `Flight from the middle` @desc Which flight happened?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of the flight`
`what now that my pair in the middle flew` what MEANS
    `what follows a flight from the middle` what

§§ `Two species, and heirs (2:5)`

@ref Kinnim 2:5
@export My sin offering and my burnt offering were of different species: what must I bring again? Answers from Kinnim 2:5.
GIVEN `my sin offering's species`   IS A `Species` @desc Was your sin offering a turtledove or a young pigeon?
      `my burnt offering's species` IS A `Species` @desc Was your burnt offering a turtledove or a young pigeon?
      `the sin offering came first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your sin offering brought before your burnt offering?
      reading                       IS A `Reading of 2:5` @desc Answer with the first view (the halakha) or with Ben Azzai?
GIVETH A `What she must bring again`
`what must I bring again for my pair of two species` `my sin offering's species` `my burnt offering's species` `the sin offering came first` reading MEANS
    `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` `my sin offering's species` `my burnt offering's species` `the sin offering came first` reading

@ref Kinnim 2:5
@export I am the heir of someone who died after one offering of their pair was brought: must I bring the other? Answers from Kinnim 2:5. Only for an heir.
GIVEN `the offering brought before the death` IS AN `Offering` @desc Which offering had been brought before they died?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must I as heir bring the other offering` `the offering brought before the death` MEANS
    `her heirs must bring the other offering of her pair` `the offering brought before the death`

§§ `My birds were mixed, and the priest offered them without asking (3:1 to 3:4): only if this happened`

@ref Kinnim 3:1-3:2
@export My unassigned pairs were mixed with other people's, and the priest offered them all without asking: at least how many of all the offerings counted? Answers in birds from Kinnim 3:1 to 3:2, reading "the majority" with Koppel and Reiss; nothing for a split the text does not name.
GIVEN `my pairs`        IS A NUMBER @desc How many pairs did you bring, without saying which bird was which?
      `the other pairs` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each other owner whose pairs were mixed with yours, how many pairs.
      what              IS A `What the priest did` @desc Did the priest offer them all above the red line, all below, half above and half below, or some other number above?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`at least how many of the mixed offerings counted` `my pairs` `the other pairs` what MEANS
    `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (`my pairs` FOLLOWED BY `the other pairs`) what

@ref Kinnim 3:2
@export The same, under another reading of "the majority is valid": at least how many of all the offerings counted, if the priest offered half above and half below? Answers in birds, or nothing where the reading does not speak to so many owners.
GIVEN `my pairs`        IS A NUMBER @desc How many pairs did you bring?
      `the other pairs` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each other owner, how many pairs.
      reading           IS A `Reading of the majority` @desc Whose reading: Koppel and Reiss, Bartenura, Tiferet Yisrael, or Maimonides?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`at least how many counted under the reading` `my pairs` `the other pairs` reading MEANS
    `the fewest offerings certainly valid, half above and half below, under the reading` (`my pairs` FOLLOWED BY `the other pairs`) reading

@ref Kinnim 3:1-3:2
@export How many pairs must we, the owners, bring again between us? Answers from Kinnim 3:1 to 3:2 as Bartenura and Ravad read it: the birds not certainly valid, brought jointly.
GIVEN `my pairs`        IS A NUMBER @desc How many pairs did you bring?
      `the other pairs` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each other owner, how many pairs.
      what              IS A `What the priest did` @desc What did the priest do?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`how many pairs must we bring again between us` `my pairs` `the other pairs` what MEANS
    `the pairs the owners must bring again together` (`my pairs` FOLLOWED BY `the other pairs`) what

@ref Maimonides, Pesulei ha-Mukdashin 8:6-7
@export On Maimonides' reading, did all of my own offerings count, so that my obligation is met? Answers yes where my pairs are more than all the others' together; otherwise he does not say.
GIVEN `my pairs`        IS A NUMBER @desc How many pairs did you bring?
      `the other pairs` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each other owner, how many pairs.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`on Maimonides' reading, did all my offerings count` `my pairs` `the other pairs` MEANS
    `on Maimonides' reading, all of her offerings count` `my pairs` `the other pairs`

@ref Kinnim 3:3, the worst case applied beyond the text
@export Beyond the text: the priest, not asking, put some other number of the birds above. By the worst-case principle the commentators apply beyond the mishnah, at least how many counted? Not the text's own answer.
GIVEN `my pairs`         IS A NUMBER @desc How many pairs did you bring?
      `the other pairs`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each other owner, how many pairs.
      `birds put above`  IS A NUMBER @desc How many of all the birds the priest offered above the red line.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`beyond the text, at least how many counted` `my pairs` `the other pairs` `birds put above` MEANS
    `the fewest offerings certainly valid for any number above, beyond the text` (`my pairs` FOLLOWED BY `the other pairs`) `birds put above`

@ref Kinnim 3:3-3:4
@export Birds already made sin or burnt offerings were mixed with unassigned pairs, and the priest offered them without asking: at least how many counted? Answers in birds from Kinnim 3:3 to 3:4.
GIVEN `designated sin offerings`   IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the birds had already been made sin offerings?
      `designated burnt offerings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many had already been made burnt offerings?
      `unassigned pairs`           IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each owner whose pairs were not yet assigned, how many pairs (empty if none).
      what                         IS A `What the priest did` @desc What did the priest do?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`at least how many counted when assigned birds were mixed in` `designated sin offerings` `designated burnt offerings` `unassigned pairs` what MEANS
    `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` m what
    WHERE
        m MEANS `Mixture` WITH
                    `designated sin offerings`   IS `designated sin offerings`
                    `designated burnt offerings` IS `designated burnt offerings`
                    `unassigned obligations`     IS map `a nest of pairs` `unassigned pairs`

§§ `My vow for the birth of a son (3:6): only for someone who made this vow`

@ref Kinnim 3:6
@export I vowed "a pair upon me when I bear a son", bore a son, and gave both pairs to the priest, who did not offer them rightly: how many more birds must I bring? Answers from Kinnim 3:6.
GIVEN known               IS A `What is known of her vow` @desc Which is true: you did not say which birds were for your vow (and he offered two above and two below); you said which (the same); you named your vow's species when vowing and do not remember it (the same); or it is not known what you gave or what he did?
      `of two species`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your two pairs of different species (one of turtledoves, one of young pigeons)?
      `as Ben Azzai says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Answer as Ben Azzai (two sin offerings, where nothing is known)? The first view is false.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many more birds must I bring for my vow and my obligation` known `of two species` `as Ben Azzai says` MEANS
    `the more birds she must bring` known `of two species` `as Ben Azzai says`
